Upstream-bound: no
Subject: [PORT_HOST] P10.6 step 1: icon census hook in processTextChar (DW3_ICON_CENSUS=1)

Design: docs/P10.6_GLYPHS.md ("Census"). `processTextChar` case 1 (a font icon,
the bytes `01 n` or a Shift-JIS symbol found in FONT_ICON_MAP) calls
`dw3_port_icon_census` (port/options/switch_glyphs.c) with the icon number, the
text style (index in FONT.styles), the string and the position of the icon.
With the environment variable DW3_ICON_CENSUS=1 the port logs one line per
distinct (icon, style, string) with the scene (mode overlay) and the bytes
around the icon, in hex, so a scripted walk says which strings use which icon
(`dw3-icon-census:` lines). Without the variable the call is a flag test: no
log, no change to the text or to the picture. The Switch has no environment,
so it never logs there. The patch does not change what is drawn; the Switch
glyph patch itself (port/options/switch_glyphs.c) wraps FONT.load and needs no
edit of the decomp.

--- a/src/engine/text/text_window.c
+++ b/src/engine/text/text_window.c
@@ -1,6 +1,7 @@
 #include "engine/game.h"
 
 #if PORT_HOST
+#include "port_glyphs.h"
 #include "port_pacing.h"
 #endif
 
@@ -616,6 +617,10 @@
     case 1:
         style = obj->style;
         n = (u8)draw->code;
+#if PORT_HOST
+        /* P10.6 census (DW3_ICON_CENSUS=1): which icon, in which style, from which string */
+        dw3_port_icon_census(n, (s32)(style - FONT.styles), text->data, *pos, text->sjis);
+#endif
         if (n <= style->iconCount && n > 0) {
             draw->glyph = &style->icons[n - 1];
         } else {
